# SRG-APP-000175-AU-002630  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server, when utilizing PKI-based authentication, must
# validate certificates by constructing a certification path (which includes
# status information) to an accepted trust anchor.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000175-AU-002630
group:           V-206478
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000185
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk can be given a certificate authority store to build the
                 certification path to, and can be told to perform certificate status
                 validation, which is the product's share of validating a presented
                 certificate to an accepted trust anchor with status information.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod equals crl
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The content of the certificate authority store, and whether its anchors
                 are the accepted ones, is a PKI decision outside Splunk configuration
external:        Current CRL files must be present in the instance's auth/crl directory in
                 PEM format and refreshed from the issuing certificate authority, which is
                 a distribution procedure rather than a Splunk setting
external:        The requirement is Not Applicable where PKI-based authentication is not
                 used; selecting PKI authentication is assessed under
                 SRG-APP-000149-AU-002280 and SRG-APP-000150-AU-002320

citation:        SRG-APP-000175-AU-002630 check text; server.conf.spec:1125-1147
                 (certificateStatusValidationMethod: only acceptable value is crl, default
                 empty string meaning status validation is off, and it then applies to
                 Splunk Web, splunkd and Splunk-to-Splunk channels; CRL files live under
                 the instance's auth/crl directory in PEM format),
                 server.conf.spec:996-1010 (sslRootCAPath, the concatenated CA store, no
                 default), web.conf.spec:108-119 (web.conf sslRootCAPath falls back to the
                 server.conf setting of the same name)
finding:         server.conf [sslConfig] does not set certificateStatusValidationMethod =
                 crl or leaves sslRootCAPath empty, so the application does not validate
                 presented certificates to a named trust anchor with revocation status.
